00:10:06.840 --> 00:10:09.870
The story of Switzerland starts here.

00:10:09.870 --> 00:10:13.170
Well, actually down there at that lake

00:10:13.170 --> 00:10:15.329
in a little green valley where a group

00:10:15.329 --> 00:10:18.450
of people came together and made a promise

00:10:18.450 --> 00:10:20.490
to each other 700 years ago.

00:10:20.490 --> 00:10:23.823
And with that promise came a myth.

00:10:27.540 --> 00:10:29.340
The hero's name was William Tell

00:10:29.340 --> 00:10:31.710
and legend has it that one day he refused

00:10:31.710 --> 00:10:34.410
to bow down to the king's local leader.

00:10:34.410 --> 00:10:36.690
It was a daring act of disrespect.

00:10:36.690 --> 00:10:39.210
So as punishment, the overlord forced him

00:10:39.210 --> 00:10:42.270
to shoot an apple off his own son's head.

00:10:42.270 --> 00:10:45.333
Tell aimed his crossbow
carefully and released.

00:10:46.200 --> 00:10:47.880
He made the perfect shot.

00:10:47.880 --> 00:10:50.070
He continued to defy the ruler

00:10:50.070 --> 00:10:51.990
and eventually inspired the tribes

00:10:51.990 --> 00:10:54.270
in this region to launch a rebellion.

00:10:54.270 --> 00:10:56.280
Tell eventually shot the ruler dead

00:10:56.280 --> 00:10:57.300
and the rebels would go on

00:10:57.300 --> 00:10:59.760
to win their independence,
banding together

00:10:59.760 --> 00:11:03.000
to start the Confederacy that
would become Switzerland.

00:11:03.000 --> 00:11:04.680
They first made an agreement

00:11:04.680 --> 00:11:06.630
that they would protect one another,

00:11:06.630 --> 00:11:09.360
but instead of forming a
full-time standing army run

00:11:09.360 --> 00:11:11.280
by a king, they would arm

00:11:11.280 --> 00:11:13.950
and train ordinary people to fight.

00:11:13.950 --> 00:11:16.983
So not an army at all,
but rather a militia.

