00:19:22.599 --> 00:19:24.121
for you, this is like no big deal,

00:19:24.121 --> 00:19:25.380
for me, this is a giant gun.

00:19:25.380 --> 00:19:28.230
Like this is like, I don't handle guns.

00:19:28.230 --> 00:19:29.700
Like I held a gun like this

00:19:29.700 --> 00:19:31.650
for the first time like two days ago,

00:19:31.650 --> 00:19:33.042
for the very first time

00:19:33.042 --> 00:19:33.875
in my life.
- No way.

00:19:33.875 --> 00:19:35.670
- Yes, actually I'm an American.

00:19:35.670 --> 00:19:38.973
- Yeah, that's very uncliche.

00:19:39.900 --> 00:19:42.510
- Switzerland still has a militia.

00:19:42.510 --> 00:19:47.010
Every able-bodied man in
Switzerland is given a uniform

00:19:47.010 --> 00:19:50.790
and a gun and required
to join the military.

00:19:50.790 --> 00:19:53.550
- And this is in the constitution.

00:19:53.550 --> 00:19:55.920
It's written there that
every male can be forced,

00:19:55.920 --> 00:19:57.600
not only forced to do military service,

00:19:57.600 --> 00:20:00.030
but also forced to make more.

00:20:00.030 --> 00:20:03.372
So instead of 21 weeks, I did 37 weeks

00:20:03.372 --> 00:20:07.260
and in total, I have to do like 450 days.

00:20:07.260 --> 00:20:09.090
- Up until the nineties,
you would go to jail

00:20:09.090 --> 00:20:10.380
if you refused to do this.

00:20:10.380 --> 00:20:13.680
Now you just have to pay 3%
of your income if you don't,

00:20:13.680 --> 00:20:16.890
- I was also very against the military

00:20:16.890 --> 00:20:18.690
and I went reluctantly.

00:20:18.690 --> 00:20:20.234
- One of the first things you do

00:20:20.234 --> 00:20:22.320
in this initial training is
you come to one of these clubs

00:20:22.320 --> 00:20:23.430
and you learn to shoot.

00:20:23.430 --> 00:20:25.080
- It was kind of scary actually,

00:20:25.080 --> 00:20:27.870
because it's all like
18 to 20-year-old guys

00:20:27.870 --> 00:20:29.430
and just like, oh yeah, we're gonna go

00:20:29.430 --> 00:20:31.737
to shoot this gun now.

00:20:31.737 --> 00:20:35.460
And it's like, here's
ammunition, here's the rounds

00:20:35.460 --> 00:20:37.050
and now you do what you learned.

00:20:37.050 --> 00:20:39.949
- After the recruits complete
their training, they return

00:20:39.949 --> 00:20:42.990
back to their normal jobs,
to their normal lives,

00:20:42.990 --> 00:20:46.260
but they keep their firearm
with them in their home.

00:20:46.260 --> 00:20:48.420
And then they're required to come to one

00:20:48.420 --> 00:20:52.389
of these private clubs every
year to practice shooting.

00:20:52.389 --> 00:20:56.222
- (speaking foreign language)

00:20:58.590 --> 00:21:00.690
- It's called the obligatories.

00:21:00.690 --> 00:21:04.410
So it's obligatory or
mandatory for people to shoot.

00:21:04.410 --> 00:21:05.760
- This is my shooting book.

00:21:05.760 --> 00:21:07.210
You know, every time I shoot,

00:21:10.372 --> 00:21:12.960
there is like a little report,
somebody has to sign it.

00:21:12.960 --> 00:21:15.360
Of course when you go shooting,
you just take this out

00:21:15.360 --> 00:21:17.730
and then it's just like this.

00:21:17.730 --> 00:21:19.230
- Wow.

00:21:19.230 --> 00:21:21.193
- And you go to the public
transport just like that.

00:21:21.193 --> 00:21:24.960
- You're just walking around
on the train with your guns.

00:21:24.960 --> 00:21:26.520
- Yeah.
- Really?

00:21:26.520 --> 00:21:28.050
- So it's actually similar to

00:21:28.050 --> 00:21:30.960
what the United States National
Defense Strategy looked

00:21:30.960 --> 00:21:35.550
in like the 1800s where every
able-bodied man had a gun

00:21:35.550 --> 00:21:38.250
and was required to use
it, required to be ready

00:21:38.250 --> 00:21:41.700
to defend the country from
invasion or insurrection.

00:21:41.700 --> 00:21:45.480
- Part of this is also being able to fight

00:21:45.480 --> 00:21:47.670
if it will be necessary just

00:21:47.670 --> 00:21:50.184
to, you know, protect our country.

00:21:50.184 --> 00:21:53.730
And this, you know,
self-defense thinking is part

00:21:53.730 --> 00:21:57.090
of, you know, our people from Switzerland.

00:21:57.090 --> 00:21:58.700
- What Switzerland
doesn't have that we have

00:21:58.700 --> 00:22:01.530
in the United States
is a Second amendment,

00:22:01.530 --> 00:22:05.310
a articulated, unambiguous
right to have guns.

00:22:05.310 --> 00:22:07.883
Instead, guns are articulated mostly

00:22:07.883 --> 00:22:11.130
as a duty to protect the country.

00:22:11.130 --> 00:22:14.130
And then secondly comes
the privilege to use guns,

00:22:14.130 --> 00:22:16.680
to compete with them,
to own guns, et cetera.

00:22:16.680 --> 00:22:19.710
For them, the duty came first.

00:22:19.710 --> 00:22:22.680
- We have a tradition, more
of a liberty tradition,

00:22:22.680 --> 00:22:27.060
and there it's more of a
responsibility tradition.

00:22:27.060 --> 00:22:29.010
- Essentially, everybody has to go.

00:22:29.010 --> 00:22:31.200
So this is kind of like one thing

00:22:31.200 --> 00:22:34.320
that unifies a lot of
the male population here.

00:22:34.320 --> 00:22:36.450
And it's just like you can meet a guy

00:22:36.450 --> 00:22:38.760
and if he is done military
service as well, you can talk

00:22:38.760 --> 00:22:40.590
for hours and hours and hours.

00:22:40.590 --> 00:22:42.540
- And this to me, makes
all the difference,

00:22:42.540 --> 00:22:46.800
like these two different
purposes of guns in society,

00:22:46.800 --> 00:22:49.110
whether they are a right for individuals

00:22:49.110 --> 00:22:50.970
or the duty of the collective.

00:22:50.970 --> 00:22:52.530
I think this is a major factor

00:22:52.530 --> 00:22:54.660
that divides these two gun cultures.

00:22:54.660 --> 00:22:59.660
If you could describe Swiss
shooting culture in three words,

00:23:00.270 --> 00:23:02.009
what would those words be?

00:23:02.009 --> 00:23:05.842
- (speaking foreign language)

00:23:09.183 --> 00:23:10.320
- And this is where it all clicked for me.

00:23:10.320 --> 00:23:13.170
I had thought that Switzerland's
gun culture was the product

00:23:13.170 --> 00:23:15.900
of smart laws and gun policies.

00:23:15.900 --> 00:23:17.970
But being here, it was becoming clear

00:23:17.970 --> 00:23:19.710
that it was the militia system

00:23:19.710 --> 00:23:21.750
that was at the root of all of this.

00:23:21.750 --> 00:23:24.660
The requirement for every
man to learn how to shoot

00:23:24.660 --> 00:23:28.650
as the main strategy for
collective national defense,

00:23:28.650 --> 00:23:32.624
turning guns into a symbol
of community and celebration.

00:23:32.624 --> 00:23:36.360
The center of large festivals
all over the country,

00:23:36.360 --> 00:23:38.430
where Swiss traditions are celebrated

00:23:38.430 --> 00:23:41.160
with firearms at the center, like

00:23:41.160 --> 00:23:44.130
that teen shooting competition in Zurich,

00:23:44.130 --> 00:23:46.290
or this important shooting festival

00:23:46.290 --> 00:23:47.790
that takes place at the foot

00:23:47.790 --> 00:23:50.610
of the Alps along a beautiful Swiss lake.

00:23:50.610 --> 00:23:51.930
The place where the founders

00:23:51.930 --> 00:23:55.263
of Switzerland formed
their confederacy in 1291.

00:23:56.761 --> 00:24:01.110
- (speaking foreign language)

00:24:01.110 --> 00:24:03.570
- You have so many members
of the community coming out

00:24:03.570 --> 00:24:04.920
and participating in them.

00:24:04.920 --> 00:24:07.110
You're gonna have fun.
The shooting is fun.

