00:25:51.480 --> 00:25:53.713
Yes, so 300 meters away.

00:25:53.713 --> 00:25:55.744
I think that this bullet just traveled

00:25:55.744 --> 00:25:59.010
across the valley over the cars

00:25:59.010 --> 00:26:04.010
and hit a thing that's this
big is pretty satisfying.

00:26:04.380 --> 00:26:08.460
So while I'm sitting here
shooting bullseyes right below us,

00:26:08.460 --> 00:26:09.870
not only are other cars,

00:26:09.870 --> 00:26:12.510
but there's a guy just mowing the lawn.

00:26:12.510 --> 00:26:14.520
Like there's a guy mowing
the lawn right there

00:26:14.520 --> 00:26:16.050
under the shooting range.

00:26:16.050 --> 00:26:19.020
This place is at once super buttoned up

00:26:19.020 --> 00:26:22.080
when it comes to guns and
seemingly very relaxed,

00:26:22.080 --> 00:26:23.910
but it's not relaxed.

00:26:23.910 --> 00:26:26.460
As I visit these gun clubs, it's striking

00:26:26.460 --> 00:26:30.570
how much these feel like a magnet

00:26:30.570 --> 00:26:34.470
for community, a gathering
place for the community,

00:26:34.470 --> 00:26:37.093
a collective activity and competition

00:26:37.093 --> 00:26:39.750
that everyone in the community can enjoy.

00:26:39.750 --> 00:26:42.900
I'm so used to guns being
associated with danger

00:26:42.900 --> 00:26:45.980
and division and politics and fear,

00:26:45.980 --> 00:26:49.350
but here it just has such
a different feel than

00:26:49.350 --> 00:26:50.310
what I'm used to.

00:26:50.310 --> 00:26:52.740
Thank you so much. I really
appreciate your time.

00:26:52.740 --> 00:26:53.573
Thank you.

00:26:53.573 --> 00:26:54.570
This is really good.

00:26:56.100 --> 00:26:57.780
It's been a really enlightening experience

00:26:57.780 --> 00:26:59.100
visiting all these shooting ranges.

00:26:59.100 --> 00:27:00.570
And what it's taught me is

00:27:00.570 --> 00:27:03.660
that guns here in Switzerland
are a totally different

00:27:03.660 --> 00:27:05.670
thing than they are in America.

00:27:05.670 --> 00:27:07.740
Like they're a completely
different symbol.

00:27:07.740 --> 00:27:09.030
They have a very different purpose.

00:27:09.030 --> 00:27:10.290
They have a very different meaning.

00:27:10.290 --> 00:27:11.670
And that's kind of surprising to me

00:27:11.670 --> 00:27:14.675
because remember that the
United States was founded

00:27:14.675 --> 00:27:17.790
on a lot of the same
paradigms as Switzerland

00:27:17.790 --> 00:27:19.380
when it came to having a militia

00:27:19.380 --> 00:27:21.450
and having firearms in society

00:27:21.450 --> 00:27:23.580
as a form of collective defense.

00:27:23.580 --> 00:27:25.770
So to understand how
these two gun cultures

00:27:25.770 --> 00:27:29.280
so greatly diverged despite
having similar roots, you have

00:27:29.280 --> 00:27:30.294
to understand what happens

00:27:30.294 --> 00:27:33.753
after the Constitution,
after the Second Amendment.

00:27:36.210 --> 00:27:40.222
- I have the right to
protect my family and myself.

00:27:40.222 --> 00:27:42.428
(gun fires)

00:27:42.428 --> 00:27:44.100
- What do you think about
American gun culture?

00:27:44.100 --> 00:27:47.133
Like what's the view?
- (beep) bonkers.

00:27:48.000 --> 00:27:52.020
The fact that everybody
has a gun in America.

00:27:52.020 --> 00:27:52.853
It would make me feel uneasy.

00:27:52.853 --> 00:27:54.900
And I'm used to being in the proximity

00:27:54.900 --> 00:27:56.460
of guns because I'm allowed a gun.

00:27:56.460 --> 00:27:57.447
I don't know how you guys do it.

00:27:57.447 --> 00:28:00.510
- And if he tries to take
our guns, he can take them

00:28:00.510 --> 00:28:02.010
from our cold, dead hands.

00:28:02.010 --> 00:28:04.410
- There has been a
shooting at a synagogue.

00:28:04.410 --> 00:28:06.600
- Get off of my porch right now.

00:28:06.600 --> 00:28:08.790
- Gun control, all it's
gonna do is take the guns out

00:28:08.790 --> 00:28:10.170
of the people that obey the law.

00:28:10.170 --> 00:28:12.840
- Three people were killed in
Jacksonville, Florida today

00:28:12.840 --> 00:28:15.843
after what appears to be a
racially motivated hate crime.

00:28:17.790 --> 00:28:20.094
- [Johnny] So after its
independence, the US quickly learned

00:28:20.094 --> 00:28:23.970
that while a militia is
great for defense, deterrence

00:28:23.970 --> 00:28:27.777
and neutrality, it is not
good for one thing, conquest.

00:28:34.020 --> 00:28:35.460
Beginning in the 19th century,

00:28:35.460 --> 00:28:37.800
the US expanded west very quickly.

00:28:37.800 --> 00:28:39.510
They fought other European colonists

00:28:39.510 --> 00:28:41.460
and Native Americans for their land.

00:28:41.460 --> 00:28:44.250
They would eventually fight
each other in a civil war.

00:28:44.250 --> 00:28:46.410
These kinds of operations were too big

00:28:46.410 --> 00:28:49.050
for militias made up of everyday citizens.

00:28:49.050 --> 00:28:50.880
Instead, they needed to establish

00:28:50.880 --> 00:28:54.690
and fund a centralized,
professional standing army.

00:28:54.690 --> 00:28:56.220
And this was just the beginning.

00:28:56.220 --> 00:28:58.890
By the time the 1900s rolled
around, the US had grown

00:28:58.890 --> 00:29:01.020
into something that Switzerland never was

00:29:01.020 --> 00:29:04.200
and probably never will
be, an expansionist empire

00:29:04.200 --> 00:29:06.450
using its sprawling permanent military

00:29:06.450 --> 00:29:08.430
to wield influence around the globe.

00:29:08.430 --> 00:29:11.280
By the middle of the century,
it would become the largest

00:29:11.280 --> 00:29:14.253
and most powerful military
to have ever existed.

00:29:20.340 --> 00:29:23.700
Because the US had a huge
standing army, it did away

00:29:23.700 --> 00:29:26.550
with a lot of the original
laws requiring people

00:29:26.550 --> 00:29:27.960
to join the militia.

00:29:27.960 --> 00:29:30.840
And now without a duty to form a militia

00:29:30.840 --> 00:29:33.060
to protect the country from invasion

00:29:33.060 --> 00:29:35.790
and insurrection like the
Constitution said, they were left

00:29:35.790 --> 00:29:38.790
with just the second half
of this amendment, the right

00:29:38.790 --> 00:29:42.090
to bear arms and how it
should not be infringed.

00:29:42.090 --> 00:29:45.840
Guns started to become more
of a personal tool, a tool

00:29:45.840 --> 00:29:48.315
to pursue their American dream, to hunt,

00:29:48.315 --> 00:29:51.990
to protect their family, to exterminate.

00:29:51.990 --> 00:29:54.120
- It's more like the Rambo style.

00:29:54.120 --> 00:29:57.540
It's not like, I'm going
shooting at the target.

00:29:57.540 --> 00:30:01.440
You don't go shooting
somewhere in the woods

00:30:01.440 --> 00:30:03.300
or in the forest, you just don't do that.

00:30:03.300 --> 00:30:06.540
You go to a shooting range and
you get part of the community

00:30:06.540 --> 00:30:08.550
and then your goal is not just

00:30:08.550 --> 00:30:10.860
to, you know, shoot wherever there is.

00:30:10.860 --> 00:30:13.350
So your goal is to get better.

00:30:13.350 --> 00:30:15.690
And your goal is not just to shoot around.

00:30:15.690 --> 00:30:18.450
- [Johnny] Guns continued to
take on a more personal symbol

00:30:18.450 --> 00:30:20.550
in the sixties and seventies when more

00:30:20.550 --> 00:30:23.400
and more Americans were losing
trust in their government.

00:30:23.400 --> 00:30:25.020
This was also right at the time

00:30:25.020 --> 00:30:27.900
when crime was skyrocketing in America.

00:30:27.900 --> 00:30:30.692
Without this duty for collective
defense, guns became more

00:30:30.692 --> 00:30:33.300
and more a symbol of personal defense

00:30:33.300 --> 00:30:35.754
from all of this crime, personal liberty

00:30:35.754 --> 00:30:39.330
and a symbol of this growing
anti-government sentiment.

00:30:39.330 --> 00:30:41.130
And as a result, the number

00:30:41.130 --> 00:30:43.173
of guns in America soared.

00:30:44.460 --> 00:30:46.998
The NRA, which remember
after the Civil War started

00:30:46.998 --> 00:30:50.371
as a largely non-political
group that was meant

00:30:50.371 --> 00:30:53.174
to just help Americans be more responsible

00:30:53.174 --> 00:30:57.570
and better marksmen, they got
taken over in the seventies

00:30:57.570 --> 00:31:00.240
by a group of hardliners who wanted

00:31:00.240 --> 00:31:03.030
to change the agenda of the NRA, turning

00:31:03.030 --> 00:31:05.790
into a political lobbying
group that was set

00:31:05.790 --> 00:31:08.070
on reshaping the way Americans thought

00:31:08.070 --> 00:31:10.020
about the Second Amendment and making sure

00:31:10.020 --> 00:31:12.210
that no legislation ever made it through

00:31:12.210 --> 00:31:13.980
that curtailed gun rights.

00:31:13.980 --> 00:31:16.440
They began pushing an interpretation
of the Second Amendment

00:31:16.440 --> 00:31:19.440
that was about individual
protection, a right to bear arms

00:31:19.440 --> 00:31:20.760
so that you can protect yourself.

00:31:20.760 --> 00:31:22.755
And trying to de-emphasize the connection

00:31:22.755 --> 00:31:26.100
to a well-regulated militia as the purpose

00:31:26.100 --> 00:31:27.600
for this right to bear arms.

00:31:27.600 --> 00:31:29.700
- In the face of this relentless onslaught

00:31:29.700 --> 00:31:30.870
of gun control schemes,

00:31:30.870 --> 00:31:33.270
you're the reason the Second
Amendment still stands.

00:31:33.270 --> 00:31:34.620
You're the tip of the spear.

00:31:34.620 --> 00:31:36.390
- You're the ones that make it possible

00:31:36.390 --> 00:31:38.580
for us every day to defend this freedom.

00:31:38.580 --> 00:31:39.690
- And it totally worked.

00:31:39.690 --> 00:31:42.510
The Second Amendment became
more and more a guarantee

00:31:42.510 --> 00:31:45.060
that everyone can have
guns to protect themselves

00:31:45.060 --> 00:31:47.310
and their family having nothing to do

00:31:47.310 --> 00:31:48.570
with protecting the country.

00:31:48.570 --> 00:31:50.760
After all, we had the biggest
military in the world.

00:31:50.760 --> 00:31:52.020
We didn't need a militia anymore.

00:31:52.020 --> 00:31:53.569
- [Announcer] Don't let
Hillary leave you protected

00:31:53.569 --> 00:31:55.260
with nothing but a phone.

00:31:55.260 --> 00:31:57.300
The NRA Political Victory
Fund is responsible

00:31:57.300 --> 00:31:58.890
for the content of this advertising,

00:31:58.890 --> 00:32:00.540
- This interpretation of guns

00:32:00.540 --> 00:32:03.510
and the Second Amendment would
become solidified in a five

00:32:03.510 --> 00:32:06.330
to four vote in the Supreme Court in 2008

00:32:06.330 --> 00:32:07.350
when the court ruled

00:32:07.350 --> 00:32:09.540
that the Second Amendment
guaranteed people

00:32:09.540 --> 00:32:12.600
to have guns, even when those
guns have no relationship

00:32:12.600 --> 00:32:14.040
to an armed militia.

00:32:14.040 --> 00:32:16.575
So this is why the United
States has more guns

00:32:16.575 --> 00:32:19.680
than any country on Earth
because the courts have ruled

00:32:19.680 --> 00:32:24.270
that guns are an individual
right, a right to bear arms.

00:32:24.270 --> 00:32:27.780
Every year, 20,000
murders occur with a gun.

00:32:27.780 --> 00:32:31.080
Thousands of children and
teens are killed with a gun.

00:32:31.080 --> 00:32:34.680
Hundreds of deaths are caused
by gun accidents, hundreds

00:32:34.680 --> 00:32:36.480
of mass shootings

00:32:36.480 --> 00:32:39.810
and of course, the leading
cause of gun violence, suicides.

00:32:39.810 --> 00:32:42.570
Tens of thousands of lives taken with guns

00:32:42.570 --> 00:32:44.160
but we can't seem to do much about it

00:32:44.160 --> 00:32:46.964
because as long as guns
remain an individual right

00:32:46.964 --> 00:32:50.160
now deeply woven into
American identity, any effort

00:32:50.160 --> 00:32:52.403
to try to pass reasonable laws, to try

00:32:52.403 --> 00:32:55.380
to limit these countless
deaths that we have

00:32:55.380 --> 00:32:59.070
in our country will
continue to fail especially

00:32:59.070 --> 00:33:01.800
as the NRA continues to politicize guns,

00:33:01.800 --> 00:33:05.130
to use them to divide
America, to scare America,

00:33:05.130 --> 00:33:07.470
and to make us feel like
we need guns to be safe.

00:33:07.470 --> 00:33:10.710
- The facts are on our
side. Guns save lives.

00:33:10.710 --> 00:33:13.460
- And you'll never stop us
from defending our families.

00:33:17.160 --> 00:33:19.140
- [Johnny] My last visit
was an important one

00:33:19.140 --> 00:33:21.810
to this gun shop where the owner is Swiss,

00:33:21.810 --> 00:33:24.150
but is a card carrying member of the NRA

00:33:24.150 --> 00:33:26.400
and a big fan of American Gun Culture.

00:33:26.400 --> 00:33:28.380
I had to get his take on this.

00:33:28.380 --> 00:33:31.200
- These are the best
assault rifles in the world.

00:33:31.200 --> 00:33:32.940
- Really?
- These are, yes.

00:33:32.940 --> 00:33:34.620
- Wow. What what makes them so good?

00:33:34.620 --> 00:33:35.820
Why are they so good?

00:33:35.820 --> 00:33:37.973
- They're Swiss made. (laughs)

00:33:37.973 --> 00:33:39.470
Any questions?

00:33:39.470 --> 00:33:40.303
- Yeah, yeah, yeah. Exactly.

00:33:40.303 --> 00:33:42.390
You don't need to say anymore.

00:33:42.390 --> 00:33:45.303
What do you feel when you
look at American gun culture?

00:33:49.770 --> 00:33:51.183
- It's very interesting.

00:33:53.430 --> 00:33:54.480
From the gun system,

00:33:54.480 --> 00:33:57.360
from the gun laws, I would
like to live in the States

00:33:57.360 --> 00:34:00.123
but not with all the dumbasses around.

00:34:01.410 --> 00:34:05.890
I don't know why there are
so many deaths, accidents

00:34:09.990 --> 00:34:13.005
with firearms and here, nothing.

00:34:13.005 --> 00:34:14.610
I don't know why.

00:34:14.610 --> 00:34:17.520
Why all the US Citizens so stupid

00:34:17.520 --> 00:34:21.780
and let a loaded firearm
there on the table

00:34:21.780 --> 00:34:24.510
with kids 1, 2, 3 years old.

00:34:24.510 --> 00:34:25.530
I don't know why.

00:34:25.530 --> 00:34:27.663
You need some rules.

00:34:29.040 --> 00:34:32.580
Our government, they
support shooting clubs.

00:34:32.580 --> 00:34:34.560
They do support ammo.

00:34:34.560 --> 00:34:37.590
They support shooting ranges.

00:34:37.590 --> 00:34:41.730
They support the guys who are
going to a shooting range.

00:34:41.730 --> 00:34:44.921
You need rules. You need to have it.

00:34:44.921 --> 00:34:45.963
- Yeah.

00:34:49.675 --> 00:34:52.342
(ambient music)

00:35:02.460 --> 00:35:06.360
So here's my conclusion in all of this.

00:35:06.360 --> 00:35:08.640
I went into this story thinking

00:35:08.640 --> 00:35:10.950
that I was gonna tell a policy story like

00:35:10.950 --> 00:35:15.090
how different policies
would affect gun culture

00:35:15.090 --> 00:35:17.640
and it totally took a different route

00:35:17.640 --> 00:35:19.978
because I learned sort of halfway through

00:35:19.978 --> 00:35:23.195
that guns are a symbol.

00:35:23.195 --> 00:35:25.710
They're a symbol. Yes, they're a weapon.

00:35:25.710 --> 00:35:27.240
Yes, they're a sports tool,

00:35:27.240 --> 00:35:31.560
but they're also a symbol for
the people who wield them.

00:35:31.560 --> 00:35:34.114
The way we see guns is deeply influenced

00:35:34.114 --> 00:35:37.980
by the stories and the
myths of our societies.

00:35:37.980 --> 00:35:40.650
Switzerland and the United
States have two very different

00:35:40.650 --> 00:35:41.850
stories and because of

00:35:41.850 --> 00:35:44.460
that, they have two very
different gun cultures.

00:35:44.460 --> 00:35:47.340
For Switzerland, having armed
citizens who are trained

00:35:47.340 --> 00:35:50.760
with weapons is what kept
them neutral and safe

00:35:50.760 --> 00:35:52.470
as a group, as a collective.

00:35:52.470 --> 00:35:54.871
The United States admired
this and tried to copy it

00:35:54.871 --> 00:35:56.940
and they did for a while

00:35:56.940 --> 00:36:00.510
but soon the demands of an
expanding empire allowed

00:36:00.510 --> 00:36:03.060
that vision to fade and turned the meaning

00:36:03.060 --> 00:36:06.180
of guns into something
different, making it a right

00:36:06.180 --> 00:36:08.310
for individuals to protect themselves.

00:36:08.310 --> 00:36:11.820
Most guns in America are
not used to protect people.

00:36:11.820 --> 00:36:13.200
That's not what they're used for.

00:36:13.200 --> 00:36:15.510
They're often used at a
shooting range or hunting

00:36:15.510 --> 00:36:17.700
or to end someone's life.

00:36:17.700 --> 00:36:21.000
And yet to the people who
hold fast to their firearms

00:36:21.000 --> 00:36:23.640
as a right, they feel like any change

00:36:23.640 --> 00:36:25.800
to that, any legislation to change

00:36:25.800 --> 00:36:30.020
or to limit those guns is a
taking away of their right.

00:36:30.020 --> 00:36:31.650
So the way I see it, as long

00:36:31.650 --> 00:36:35.130
as guns are an individual
right, associated

00:36:35.130 --> 00:36:37.860
with personal protection
and personal liberty,

00:36:37.860 --> 00:36:40.140
not a lot's gonna change in America.

00:36:40.140 --> 00:36:41.580
We certainly don't stand a chance

00:36:41.580 --> 00:36:44.034
of having a culture, anything like

00:36:44.034 --> 00:36:46.756
what we've seen here in Switzerland.

00:36:46.756 --> 00:36:50.313
And that's a shame to me. That's a shame.

00:36:57.453 --> 00:37:00.036
(mellow music)

00:37:23.955 --> 00:37:25.110
Hey, before you go, I need
to tell you one last thing,

00:37:25.110 --> 00:37:28.020
which is that we made
probably our last batch

00:37:28.020 --> 00:37:30.330
of the poster that I designed last year.

00:37:30.330 --> 00:37:32.370
It's a poster called All Maps Are Wrong

00:37:32.370 --> 00:37:33.750
and I'm very proud of it.

00:37:33.750 --> 00:37:36.360
It shows all the ways that
you can take our earth

00:37:36.360 --> 00:37:38.760
and project it onto a 2D plane,

00:37:38.760 --> 00:37:41.070
which always comes with some distortion.

00:37:41.070 --> 00:37:43.140
Anyway, it's kind of a
nerdy map lover thing

00:37:43.140 --> 00:37:44.430
and if you're into
that, you should go over

00:37:44.430 --> 00:37:46.757
and check it out before they're all gone.

00:37:46.757 --> 00:37:48.080
This is probably gonna be our last batch,

00:37:48.080 --> 00:37:50.903
so get 'em while they last and
the links in the description.

